Every morning, Oliver would rise before the sun, his footsteps echoing through the quiet halls of the hospice. He was meticulous in his work, ensuring that each patient's room was spotless, their belongings arranged with care, and their personal preferences honored. His gentle touch and soothing voice brought a sense of calm to the often chaotic environment.

